{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>You shall not die.</b> Rashi's explanation: he pushed her until she touched it; he said to her: just as you do not die by touching, etc. And if you ask: how did he know that she would not die from touching — the day had not yet passed, and the Merciful One said 'for on the day you eat of it you shall surely die'? But one should not question the words of our rabbis of blessed memory. But to answer the heretics, one may say that the serpent spoke with her on the following day; he pushed her and said: just as there is no death by touching, etc. — for the day had already passed — and he induced her, and she ate from the tree of knowledge on that second day after the touching, and she also gave to her husband. Another interpretation: <b>you shall not die.</b> The serpent said to Eve: eat of it and you will thereby lose nothing, for in any event death has already been decreed upon you through the touching, so what will you lose if you eat of it? And this is the meaning of <b>you shall not die</b>: it is not on account of the eating alone that you shall die, for death has already been decreed upon you on account of the touching."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:02:38.695296749Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}